      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition: Why Heartbeat",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==NATs==, load balancers and proxies **silently** drop idle TCP",
            "No FIN, no RST: both sides think the link is alive",
            "A dead peer can go unnoticed for __minutes__",
            "Heartbeat = send a ping on a timer and expect a pong back"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: Ping and Pong Frames",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Frame",
            "Opcode",
            "Rule"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ping",
              "`0x9`",
              "peer **must** answer"
            ],
            [
              "pong",
              "`0xA`",
              "echoes ==same payload=="
            ],
            [
              "unsolicited pong",
              "`0xA`",
              "one-way keepalive"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "websockets: `ping_interval=20`, `ping_timeout=20` by default",
            "No pong within the timeout → close with ==1011==",
            "1011 reason: __keepalive ping timeout__ (codes: page 5)",
            "Control frames can arrive between the fragments of a message"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: Configure and Measure",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "serve(handler, \"\", 8765,",
            "      ping_interval=20,",
            "      ping_timeout=20)",
            "# manual ping = RTT probe",
            "pong = await ws.ping()",
            "latency = await pong  # seconds"
          ],
          "note": "ping() returns a future; await it"
        },
