        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Proxies, Browsers & TCP",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "nginx `proxy_read_timeout` (60s default) **must** exceed the ping interval",
            "Browser JS can't send ping frames → app-level `{\"type\":\"ping\"}`",
            "==TCP keepalive== (~2 h default) is far too slow",
            "Use WebSocket-level pings to catch dead peers"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Pick 20–30s",
          "text": "Shorter intervals detect failures faster but cost ==wakeups== and traffic across **10k+** connections."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "Detecting dead links"
