    {
      "page_title": "Backpressure and Bounded Queues",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is backpressure",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==Backpressure==: a slow consumer must **slow down** the producer. Without it, buffers grow without limit until the process runs out of memory (OOM).",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism in websockets",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Side",
            "Knob",
            "Default",
            "When full"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Send",
              "`write_limit`",
              "32 KiB",
              "`send()` waits"
            ],
            [
              "Receive",
              "`max_queue`",
              "16 msgs",
              "stops reading"
            ],
            [
              "TCP",
              "window",
              "kernel",
              "sender blocks"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`await ws.send()` waits past the ==high-water mark==",
            "Always **await** send: that wait *is* the backpressure",
            "Full `max_queue` → library stops reading the socket",
            "TCP flow control then pushes back on the {blue:sender}"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Template: bounded queue",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "q = asyncio.Queue(maxsize=100)",
            "await q.put(x)  # blocks if full",
            "try:",
            "    q.put_nowait(x)",
            "except asyncio.QueueFull:",
            "    ...  # apply drop policy"
          ],
          "note": "never unbounded Queue() on hot paths"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Policy",
            "How",
            "Fits"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Drop newest",
              "skip x",
              "stale-ok ticks"
            ],
            [
              "Drop oldest",
              "get_nowait → put",
              "prices, cursors"
            ],
            [
              "Keep one slot",
              "maxsize=1",
              "latest value"
            ],
            [
              "Block",
              "`await q.put`",
              "chat, event logs"
            ],
            [
              "Disconnect",
              "close 1008/1013",
              "chat, event logs"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Pick by data type",
          "text": "==Latest-value== data (prices, cursors) → drop old or keep one slot. Event logs / chat → **block** or disconnect with 1008/1013."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example: per-client writer",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "producer",
                "ink": "black"
              },
              {
                "text": "bounded queue",
                "sub": "one per client",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "writer task",
                "sub": "one per client",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "ws.send()",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def writer(ws, q):",
            "    while True:",
            "        m = await q.get()",
            "        await asyncio.wait_for(",
            "            ws.send(m), timeout=5)"
          ],
          "note": "on TimeoutError: close the client"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Core loop: `await ws.send(await q.get())`",
            "Guard slow sends with `wait_for(..., timeout=5)`",
            "Timeout → **close** that client so it can't stall others",
            "Fan-out to many clients: see page 7"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`create_task(ws.send(m))` per message (fire-and-forget)",
            "…this ==hides errors== and **discards** backpressure",
            "Unbounded `Queue()` on a hot path → OOM",
            "Calling `send()` without await, or with no timeout"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "slow consumers, safe buffers"
    },
