      "page_title": "Broadcast Registry & Fan-out Methods",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Mechanism: The Registry",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "clients: set = set()",
            "async def handler(ws):",
            "    clients.add(ws)",
            "    try: await ws.wait_closed()",
            "    finally: clients.discard(ws)"
          ],
          "note": "finally runs on every disconnect"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Registry== = a `set` of live connections",
            "`add` inside **try**, `discard` inside finally, so no entry leaks",
            "Rooms: `dict[str, set[ws]]` maps each topic to its subscribers",
            "Delete a room when its set is **empty**, or keys pile up"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "rooms: dict[str, set] = {}",
            "rooms.setdefault(t, set()).add(ws)",
            "rooms[t].discard(ws)",
            "if not rooms[t]: del rooms[t]"
          ],
          "note": "empty room = leaked key"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Example: Queue Fan-out",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "data = json.dumps(msg)  # ONCE",
            "for ws in list(clients):  # copy",
            "    try: queues[ws].put_nowait(data)",
            "    except asyncio.QueueFull:",
            "        policy(ws)  # drop / close"
          ],
          "note": "bounded queue per client"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each client has a ==writer task==: `await ws.send(await q.get())`",
            "The writer applies its **own** drop/disconnect policy (see page 6)",
            "Serialize once, then fan out: O(N) writes per message",
            "`list(clients)` is a **snapshot**, so the set can change safely"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Comparison: 4 Ways",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Waits?",
            "Slow client"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`for ws: await send`",
              "serial",
              "**stalls all**"
            ],
            [
              "`gather(..., return_exceptions=True)`",
              "concurrent",
              "slowest = finish"
            ],
            [
              "`broadcast(conns, m)`",
              "no (sync)",
              "skipped"
            ],
            [
              "queue + writer",
              "no",
              "own policy"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "websockets.asyncio.server.broadcast",
          "text": "Synchronous, so **no await**. It writes without waiting and skips clients that are closed or backed up."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Publisher",
                "sub": "any worker"
              },
              {
                "text": "Redis pub/sub",
                "sub": "redis.asyncio / NATS",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "Worker A, B, C",
                "sub": "subscribe"
              },
              {
                "text": "Local clients",
                "sub": "fan out",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A worker's registry only sees **its own** process",
            "With many processes/hosts: publish to ==Redis pub/sub== or NATS",
            "Each worker fans the message out to its local set"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "one message, N sockets"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Broadcast Pitfalls & Picking a Strategy",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "from websockets.asyncio.server \\",
            "    import broadcast",
            "data = json.dumps(msg)",
            "broadcast(clients, data)  # sync"
          ],
          "note": "no await; skips closed/backed-up"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 4. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`for ws in clients: await ws.send(m)`: one slow client stalls **everyone**",
            "Iterating the live set: 'set changed size during iteration'",
            "`json.dumps` inside the loop: N× the serialization work",
            "No `discard` in finally: dead sockets stay in the registry",
            "Expecting `gather` to be fast: the **slowest** client still sets the finish time"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 5. Example: gather vs broadcast",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "data = json.dumps(msg)",
            "await asyncio.gather(",
            "  *(ws.send(data)",
            "    for ws in list(clients)),",
            "  return_exceptions=True)"
          ],
          "note": "slowest client sets the finish time"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 6. Pick a Strategy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "few clients, all fast",
              "`gather`"
            ],
            [
              "latest-value ticks",
              "`broadcast()`"
            ],
            [
              "must not lose events",
              "queue + writer"
            ],
            [
              "many workers / hosts",
              "==Redis pub/sub=="
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Check return_exceptions",
          "text": "`gather(..., return_exceptions=True)` returns errors as values: scan them and **discard** those sockets from the registry."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 7. Example: Redis Across Workers",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "ps = redis.pubsub()",
            "await ps.subscribe(\"chat\")",
            "async for m in ps.listen():",
            "  if m[\"type\"] == \"message\":",
            "    broadcast(clients, m[\"data\"])"
          ],
          "note": "runs once per worker process"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Publish side: `await redis.publish(\"chat\", data)`",
            "Use `redis.asyncio`, never the **blocking** client",
            "Every worker gets the message, fans out ==locally==",
            "Skip non-`message` events (subscribe confirmations)"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 8. Rooms: Topic Broadcast",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def to_room(t, msg):",
            "  subs = rooms.get(t, set())",
            "  data = json.dumps(msg)",
            "  broadcast(list(subs), data)"
          ],
          "note": "missing room = no subscribers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Registry set, `discard` in **finally**",
            "Snapshot with `list()` before any fan-out",
            "==Serialize once==, reuse the string for all",
            "Delete empty rooms; Redis for multi-worker"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "one message, N sockets"
    },
