      "page_title": "Close Codes & Backoff with Jitter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Definition: Close Handshake",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "A sends close frame",
                "sub": "code + reason ≤123 B",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "B echoes close",
                "sub": "same code back",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "server closes TCP",
                "sub": "clean shutdown",
                "ink": "black"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Meaning",
            "When"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1000",
              "normal",
              "done, bye"
            ],
            [
              "1001",
              "going away",
              "shutdown / navigation"
            ],
            [
              "1002",
              "protocol error",
              "bad frame"
            ],
            [
              "1003",
              "unsupported data",
              "wrong type"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Meaning",
            "Retry?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1008",
              "policy (auth)",
              "**no**, fix creds"
            ],
            [
              "1009",
              "message too big",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "1011",
              "internal error",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "1012",
              "service restart",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "1013",
              "try again later",
              "yes"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "1006 & 4xxx",
          "items": [
            "==1006== is **never** sent on the wire",
            "local report: TCP died, no close frame",
            "==4000–4999== = your app, e.g. 4001 token expired",
            "`await ws.close(code=4001, reason=\"expired\")`"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Mechanism: Backoff",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{green:Retry}: 1001 · 1006 · 1011 · 1012 · 1013",
            "{red:Don't retry blindly}: 1008 or 4xxx auth",
            "fix credentials **first**, then reconnect",
            "==full jitter== spreads clients → no thundering herd"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "import random",
            "BASE, CAP = 1, 30  # seconds",
            "def delay(attempt):",
            "  return random.uniform(0,",
            "    min(CAP, BASE * 2**attempt))"
          ],
          "note": "random 0..ceiling, not fixed delay"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "attempt",
            "ceiling",
            "delay"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "0",
              "1s",
              "0–1s"
            ],
            [
              "1",
              "2s",
              "0–2s"
            ],
            [
              "3",
              "8s",
              "0–8s"
            ],
            [
              "5",
              "32→30s",
              "__0–30s__"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Reset rule",
          "text": "Reset `attempt = 0` only after the link stays **stable** a while (e.g. 60s), not right after the handshake."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**re-authenticate** on every new socket",
            "**re-subscribe** to your channels",
            "resume from ==last seen message id==",
            "→ no events lost across the gap"
          ],
          "style": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 4. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "retrying 1008 / 4001 in a loop, same bad token",
            "fixed delay, no jitter → thundering herd",
            "resetting attempt right after handshake",
            "sending 1006 yourself; reason over 123 bytes",
            "reconnecting without resume → lost events"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async for ws in connect()` yields a **new** socket per retry",
            "Catch `ConnectionClosed` inside, then `continue`",
            "Send auth + `last_id` first: ==resume==, no lost events",
            "`break` out of the loop to stop reconnecting"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "close, retry, resume"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Auto-Reconnect, App Codes & Resume",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Example: Auto-Reconnect",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async for ws in connect(URI):",
            "  try:",
            "    await ws.send(auth(token))",
            "    await ws.send(sub(last_id))",
            "    async for m in ws: handle(m)",
            "  except ConnectionClosed:",
            "    continue  # next retry"
          ],
          "note": "connect() loop has built-in backoff"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 5. Example: Closing with App Codes",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "if expired(token):",
            "  await ws.close(code=4001,",
            "    reason=\"expired\")  # ≤123 B",
            "# peer sees code 4001:",
            "# refresh token, then reconnect"
          ],
          "note": "never send 1006 yourself"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Exception",
            "Codes",
            "Action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`ConnectionClosedOK`",
              "1000 / 1001",
              "stop or reconnect"
            ],
            [
              "`ConnectionClosedError`",
              "1006 / 1011 / …",
              "==backoff== + retry"
            ],
            [
              "`e.rcvd.code` 1008 / 4xxx",
              "auth",
              "**fix creds** first"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 6. Server Side: Which Code?",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Send"
          ],
