      "page_title": "Server-Sent Events: Wire Format & FastAPI",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. What is SSE",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==SSE== is **one** HTTP response with `Content-Type: text/event-stream` that stays open. The server keeps pushing text events down it.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Browser `EventSource` reconnects **automatically** after the `retry:` delay",
            "On reconnect it sends a ==Last-Event-ID== header with the last `id:`",
            "Server resumes from that id, so no events are lost"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Wire Format"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            ": keepalive   <- comment",
            "retry: 3000",
            "id: 42",
            "event: token",
            "data: hello",
            ""
          ],
          "note": "a blank line ends each event"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Line",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`event:`",
              "event type name"
            ],
            [
              "`data:`",
              "payload text"
            ],
            [
              "`id:`",
              "resume cursor"
            ],
            [
              "`retry:`",
              "reconnect delay, ms"
            ],
            [
              "`: ...`",
              "comment = ==heartbeat=="
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. FastAPI Template",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def gen(req):",
            "  try:",
            "    while not await req.is_disconnected():",
            "      yield f\"data: {await nxt()}\\n\\n\"",
            "  finally:",
            "    await cleanup()  # always runs"
          ],
          "note": "finally runs on CancelledError/GeneratorExit"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@app.get(\"/stream\")",
            "async def stream(req: Request):",
            "  return StreamingResponse(",
            "    gen(req),",
            "    media_type=\"text/event-stream\")"
          ],
          "note": "gen must be an async generator"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 4. Libraries & Proxies"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "sse-starlette",
          "items": [
            "`return EventSourceResponse(gen())`",
            "sends **ping** comments for you",
            "handles disconnects automatically",
            "formats `event:`/`data:`/`id:` from yielded dicts"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# aiohttp equivalent",
            "resp = web.StreamResponse()",
            "await resp.prepare(req)",
            "await resp.write(b\"data: x\\n\\n\")",
            "return resp"
          ],
          "note": "set content_type before prepare()"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Proxies **buffer** by default: send `X-Accel-Buffering: no`",
            "Forgetting `Cache-Control: no-cache` on the stream",
            "Leaving ==gzip== on, which batches the events",
            "HTTP/1.1: only **6** connections per domain, so the 7th tab hangs",
            "Fix: ==HTTP/2== multiplexing removes the cap"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "If only the server talks, use ==SSE==: it works through HTTP infrastructure and reconnects by itself. If the client talks back too, use a WebSocket."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "fastapi",
      "subtitle": "one-way HTTP push"
