          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 6. Resume with Last-Event-ID",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def replay(req):",
            "  last = req.headers.get(",
            "    \"last-event-id\", \"0\")",
            "  for e in since(int(last)):",
            "    yield (f\"id: {e.id}\\n\"",
            "           f\"data: {e.data}\\n\\n\")"
          ],
          "note": "then continue with live events"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Give **every** event an `id:` line",
            "`EventSource` sends ==Last-Event-ID== on reconnect",
            "Replay events after that id, then go live",
            "Tune the reconnect wait with `retry: 3000`"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 7. Example: LLM Token Stream",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def tokens(prompt):",
            "  async for t in llm(prompt):",
            "    yield f\"data: {t}\\n\\n\"",
            "  yield \"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\""
          ],
          "note": "[DONE] tells the client to close"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Tab closed → generator gets ==CancelledError==",
